sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch04-18> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch04-18--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch04-18--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch04-18: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.79" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.793"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/mixed" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Both sides of the claimed correspondence are explicit: a trigonometric zero set and a substitution rule read off a continued fraction. Long numerical comparisons are routine, and the underlying combinatorics is the standard theory of mechanical words for two irrational frequencies. A mismatch of the stated formula would refute this wording even if a nearby formula were true, so the test discriminates the claim as written." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: For a range of alpha, compute the sign changes of sin(x) + sin(alpha x) and compare them with the generalized substitution system driven by the continued-fraction terms of (alpha-1)/(alpha+1). Systematic mismatch refutes the identity; agreement on long prefixes, together with the Sturmian coding of two-frequency crossings, confirms it. Quadratic irrationals should additionally yield nested patterns." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Crossings that fall extremely close to zero need validated numerics so that a rounding error is not counted as a mismatch.", "The exact prefactor (alpha-1)/(alpha+1) might differ from the classical slope coding by a transformation that has to be checked rather than assumed." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch04-18--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch04-18--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch04-18--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of wolfram2002-ch04-18 by Grok 4.7: 0.85" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.85"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch04-18--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch04-18> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch04-18--grok--operationalizability> .
